  "implementation": [
    "The invitation freezes bounded server policy (default30 seconds, maximum300). Confirmed last-Connection loss arms one durable millisecond deadline; polling/restart never renews it. Packet silence does not imply loss. First public Session activation still requires actual readiness; continuing connectivity uses sealed adapter activation custody.",
    "A current admitted native offer/answer in flight keeps the Session active across expiry. Original expiry, runtime, credential, signing key, Device/endpoint, membership epoch, source audience and recipient ceiling remain current requirements. Confirmed reconnection clears the deadline and preserves SID.",
    "Preparation and wire admission both refuse a new offer once an expired boundary has no valid Connection or negotiation, including the window before the timer runs. Explicit end on settled connections is immediate. Grace expiry is one atomic terminal transaction with code408/reconnect-grace-expired and no caller correlation.",
    "Immutable terminal facts capture their audience epochs and enter the existing source-ordered outbox. Physical recipients independently reacquire current source/key/credential/epoch/ceiling authority; catch-up reuses original facts with fresh typed envelope IDs. The boundary worker releases authority before bounded Core teardown and retries owned cleanup.",
    "Both signatures cover actual30-second expiry, active before deadline, one ended fact/hint, no new late Connection/effect and a successful new invitation; two-second same-SID reconnect/silence/explicit end and pending negotiation; five-second owned restart with changed30-second future policy and exact original deadline."
